 "source_file": "harness/results/callo_v0.3/plate/concurrency.json",
 "readme_limit": "When a reserved slot is busy with a request Callo did not send, Callo moves the classification to the lowest-id idle slot (the fallback). That helps against a foreign decode, not a foreign prefill: llama-server fills each batch in slot-id order, so with a foreign 32k prefill in slot 0 a classification moved to slot 1 starves behind it just as one left on slot 0 waits for it: measured p50 39.2 s with fallback vs 41.0 s without (the prefill took 42.1 s).",
 "subtitle": "A long agent prefill still costs seconds: 2.2 s p50 at 32k, 3.3 s at 128k (Qwen3.5-9B).",
 "fine_print": [
  {
   "lead": "Qwen3.5-9B-Q8_0, llama.cpp b50-4ebdf2c, 2026-10-02.",
   "text": "callo v0.1 bench/acceptance.py; parallel 6 (1 reserved + 5 agent slots) for decode, 4 (1 reserved) for prefill; max_tokens 128."
  },
  {
   "lead": null,
   "text": "Solos from another session (a think calibration's budget 0, the same model file, 2026-10-08)."
  },
  {
   "lead": null,
   "text": "A foreign prefill in the reserved slot itself still blocks: 31–39 s, not plotted (Qwen3.5-9B: p50 39.2 s with the S1 fallback, 41.0 s without; Tiel-Coder 35B-A3B on Callo 0.3.0, 2026-10-11: p50 30.6 s with, 31.7 s without)."
  }
 ],
 "made": [
